1
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Leave no man behind.

2
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Black Hawk Down is a action, war, history film directed by Ridley Scott.

3
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Rangers and an elite Delta Force team attempt to kidnap two underlings of a Somali warlord, their Black Hawk helicopters are
shot down, and the Americans suffer heavy casualties, facing intense fighting from the militia on the ground.

4
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
SSG Matthew Eversmann, played by Josh Hartnett.

5
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:21,000
SFC Norm 'Hoot' Gibson, played by Eric Bana.

6
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
SPC John Grimes, played by Ewan McGregor.

7
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:51,000
LTC Danny McKnight, played by Tom Sizemore.

8
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
SFC Jeff Sanderson, played by William Fichtner.

9
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:21,000
MG William F. Garrison, played by Sam Shepard.

10
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:36,000
Black Hawk Down is a 2001 war film directed and produced by Ridley Scott, and
co-produced by Jerry Bruckheimer, from a screenplay by Ken Nolan.

11
01:19:45,000 --> 01:19:51,000
It is based on the 1999 eponymous non-fiction book by journalist Mark Bowden, about the crew
of a Black Hawk helicopter that was shot down during the Battle of Mogadishu.

12
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:06,000
The film features a large ensemble cast, including Josh Hartnett, Ewan McGregor, Eric Bana, Tom Sizemore, William Fichtner, Jason
Isaacs, Sam Shepard, Jeremy Piven, Ioan Gruffudd, Ewen Bremner, Hugh Dancy, and Tom Hardy in his first film role.

13
01:34:15,000 --> 01:34:21,000
Orlando Bloom, Ty Burrell, and Nikolaj Coster-Waldau also have minor roles.

14
01:41:30,000 --> 01:41:36,000
Black Hawk Down was produced by Columbia Pictures, Revolution Studios, Jerry Bruckheimer Films and Scott Free Productions and distributed
by Sony Pictures Releasing, and had a limited release on December 28, 2001, and went into the public on January 18, 2002.

15
01:48:45,000 --> 01:48:51,000
The film received positive reviews from film critics,
although it was criticized for inaccuracies.

16
01:56:00,000 --> 01:56:06,000
It performed modestly well at the box office, grossing $172 million
worldwide against a production budget of $92 million.

17
02:03:15,000 --> 02:03:21,000
Black Hawk Down won two Academy Awards for Best Film Editing
and Best Sound at the 74th Academy Awards.

18
02:10:30,000 --> 02:10:36,000
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
ambush, chaos, militia, prisoner of war.

19
02:17:45,000 --> 02:17:51,000
The tone is intense.
